1312	// One shared scheduling step for the synchronous and asynchronous entries.
1313	// pickReadyNode already encodes activation plus dependency gating; this adds
1314	// the rules the two entries used to duplicate:
1315	// - a ready node is recorded in the trace the moment it enters execution, so
1316	//   waiting and never-activated nodes never appear in trace or output;
1317	// - an end node records its result and completes, but never stops the other
1318	//   activated branches — the caller simply loops again;
1319	// - with no ready node left, activated-but-waiting nodes classify the run as
1320	//   "blocked", a visited end node as "completed", and anything else is a
1321	//   structural cycle (validation rejects those before execution).
